+++ b/PERFORMANCE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+Client-side performance monitoring runs from `performance-monitor.js` on the
+homepage. Navigation links, Order Now, and clicks anywhere within a Seasonal
+Favorites card are labeled using `data-performance-*` attributes. Link behavior
+is unchanged.
+
+Metrics are available through `window.dailyGrindPerformance.getMetrics()` (the
+latest 100 records), User Timing measures prefixed with `daily-grind:`, and a
+`daily-grind:performance` window event. No data is sent over the network.
+
+```js
+window.addEventListener('daily-grind:performance', ({ detail }) => {
+  // Send detail to your application's telemetry collector if desired.
+  console.log(detail.name, detail.duration, detail.source);
+});
+```
+
+Durations are milliseconds. Native Event Timing includes time from the click's
+timestamp through input processing and the next paint. When native entries are
+unavailable (including interactions below the browser's 16ms reporting threshold),
+two animation frames estimate a paint opportunity; `source` distinguishes
+`event-timing` from `animation-frame-estimate`. Estimates can include an extra
+frame and cannot prove compositor presentation or completion of later async work.
+Hidden-page measurements are discarded.
+
+There is currently no client-side router or view switcher. When adding one, wrap
+its render operation with the provided API. Resolve the callback only after DOM
+updates are committed, including asynchronous data loading or framework rendering:
+
+```js
+const result = await window.dailyGrindPerformance.measureViewSwitch('menu', async () => {
+  const data = await loadMenu();
+  await renderMenu(data);
+  return data;
+});
+```
+
+This measures from the start of the update through a subsequent paint opportunity
+and emits a `view-switch` metric. Failed updates propagate their error without a
+success metric. It does not infer render completion from URL changes. Click
+metrics cover the current document's next paint; full document navigation may
+unload before a metric is available and destination loading is outside their scope.
+
+Run the deterministic Node checks with `node --test performance-monitor.test.cjs`.
+They simulate scheduling and native entries; they do not launch a browser/server
+or validate real compositor timing.
